  <note><content>
    <p>RK22 was frozen before model fitting and uses 154 Kudla measurements aggregated to 150 exact-CDS groups, with 10 seeds and five-fold out-of-fold evaluation; the tagged analysis uses 72 measurements aggregated to 71 exact-CDS groups.</p>
    <p>Adding measured 5-prime MFE increases mean HistGB out-of-fold Spearman from 0.455130 to 0.717246 and reduces MSE from 0.147232 to 0.085159; Ridge increases Spearman from minus 0.039653 to 0.678782 and reduces MSE from 0.174779 to 0.090442.</p>
    <p>All four primary structure-increment endpoints are positive in 10 of 10 seeds, exclude zero in their bootstrap intervals and have Holm-adjusted p equal to 0.0078125; the HistGB Spearman gain is 0.262115 with interval 0.230765 to 0.292225.</p>
    <p>The paired leader analysis gives Spearman 0.565992 with interval 0.378594 to 0.706085, and the CAI/GC/GC3-adjusted MFE-change coefficient is 0.098815 with interval 0.064230 to 0.133576; both tagged endpoints pass, without inventing tagged CAI or GC changes.</p>
    <p>Independent verification passed 63 of 63 checks, including every out-of-fold prediction and randomization array. This is fixed-GFP development evidence, not protein OOD, velocity, decay, functional untouched, CodonFlow-RK or SOTA evidence; RK-G1 remains false and generator training remains unauthorized (protocol commit 48eea1e2bd194b80e9c169e9420a3185e65fcb85; verified evidence commit b506bf4deca5eb229bf683ceb7ebb12ef1141833).</p>
  </content></note>
